## Test Location and Tooling

All API tests live in `apps/api/tests/`. Jest is configured via `apps/api/jest.config.js` using `ts-jest` with commonjs interop.

## Mocking Strategy

Mock `bookService` at the module level using:

```ts
jest.mock('../src/services/bookService')
```

Do not mock `fileStore` directly in route tests. The boundary is the service, not the data layer.

## No Real Data Files

Never read from or write to `/data/*.json` in any test. Define all fixture data as inline objects in the test file.

## Coverage Requirements for New Endpoints

When adding tests for a new endpoint, cover all four cases:
1. Success (correct status code and response shape)
2. Each validation or bad-input error (400 with `details` array for POST body errors)
3. Not found (404)
4. Write failure — where the service method can throw `ApiError(500, ...)`)

## Known Placeholder Stubs

`GET /api/health` and `GET /api/books` suites in `books.test.ts` are empty `describe` blocks with no assertions. Do not leave them empty when either endpoint is modified — replace with real tests at that point.

## Missing Tests

`DELETE /api/books/:id` is fully implemented but has no test coverage. Write tests before modifying that endpoint.
